    <header class="top">
      <div class="crumb"><span class="jd">32.09</span><span>Internal Tools and Systems</span><span class="sep">/</span><b>Desktop &amp; offline</b></div>
      <div class="search"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m16.5 16.5 4 4"/></svg><span>Search everything</span><span class="k">⌘K</span></div>
      <div class="tacts">
        <span class="b i dot">this device · macOS · last sync 2026-08-25 07:58</span>
        <button class="btn"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 4v6h6M20 20v-6h-6"/><path d="M20 9A8 8 0 0 0 5.6 5.6M4 15a8 8 0 0 0 14.4 3.4"/></svg>Sync now</button>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="body">
      <div class="phead">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Selective sync · classification enforced by the schema</p>
          <h1>What this device keeps offline</h1>
          <p class="lede">Field staff in low-connectivity countries are the driving case, not a nice-to-have. Financial and donor data never reaches a laptop — that is a property of the data classification, not a setting someone remembered to switch off.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sp"></div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:20px">
          <div class="kpi"><span class="l">Local pages</span><span class="v">1,001</span><span class="d">3 areas selected</span></div>
          <div class="kpi"><span class="l">Vault on disk</span><span class="v">412 MB</span><span class="d">plain markdown</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="row" style="align-items:flex-start">
        <div class="card" style="flex:1;min-width:0">
          <div class="chd"><h2>Areas kept locally</h2><div class="r"><span class="sub">you replicate only what you can read; a revoked grant purges on next connect</span></div></div>
          <div class="cbd flush">
            <table class="tbl">
              <thead><tr><th style="width:52px">Sync</th><th>Area</th><th>Classification</th><th class="num">Pages</th><th class="num">Tasks</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <sc-for list="{{areas}}" as="a" hint-placeholder-count="8">
                  <tr class="{{a.cls}}">
                    <td><button onClick="{{a.toggle}}"><span class="{{a.swCls}}"><i></i></span></button></td>
                    <td><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px"><span class="jd">{{a.range}}</span><span style="font-weight:700">{{a.name}}</span></div></td>
                    <td><span class="b {{a.clTone}}">{{a.classification}}</span></td>
                    <td class="num">{{a.pages}}</td>
                    <td class="num">{{a.tasks}}</td>
                    <td style="color:#5A6E7A;font-size:11.5px">{{a.note}}</td>
                  </tr>
                </sc-for>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <sc-if value="{{blocked}}" hint-placeholder-val="{{ true }}">
            <div class="cbd" style="border-top:1px solid #E7EEF2">
              <div class="gate">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 11h14v10H5z"/><path d="M8 11V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v4"/></svg>
                <div><b>Not offline-eligible.</b> {{blockedText}}</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </sc-if>
          <div class="prov"><span>Offline eligibility is declared per module and enforced by the schema</span><span>·</span><span class="mono">data_classification · offline_eligibility</span></div>
        </div>

        <div style="width:340px;flex:0 0 340px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px">
          <div class="card">
            <div class="chd"><h2>What works without a network</h2></div>
            <div class="cbd" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0">
              <sc-for list="{{caps}}" as="c" hint-placeholder-count="6">
                <div style="display:flex;gap:10px;padding:7px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #F1F5F8">
                  <span class="b {{c.tone}}" style="height:17px">{{c.state}}</span>
                  <div><div style="font-weight:700;font-size:12.5px">{{c.name}}</div><div style="color:#5A6E7A;font-size:11px;font-weight:600">{{c.note}}</div></div>
                </div>
              </sc-for>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <div class="chd"><h2>Markdown vault</h2><div class="r"><span class="b c">enabled</span></div></div>
            <div class="cbd" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:9px">
              <div style="font-size:12.5px;color:#3A4A53">One plain <span class="mono">.md</span> file per page, frontmatter included. Any local tool — an editor, grep, a coding agent — can read and edit the corpus, and the app feeds those edits back through the same merge path.</div>
              <div class="mono" style="background:#F7FBFD;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:9px;font-size:10.5px;color:#3A4A53;line-height:1.7">
                ~/uw-vault/<br>
                &nbsp;&nbsp;62-field-operations/<br>
                &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;63.11-chad-cluster-translation.md<br>
                &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;63.96-impact-stories/<br>
                &nbsp;&nbsp;71-content-training/
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <div class="chd"><h2>Pending reconciliation</h2><div class="r"><span class="b k">{{nPending}} queued</span></div></div>
            <div class="cbd" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0">
              <sc-for list="{{pending}}" as="p" hint-placeholder-count="3">
                <div style="display:flex;gap:10px;padding:7px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #F1F5F8">
                  <span class="b {{p.tone}}" style="height:17px">{{p.kind}}</span>
                  <div><div style="font-weight:700;font-size:12.5px">{{p.name}}</div><div style="color:#5A6E7A;font-size:11px;font-weight:600">{{p.note}}</div></div>
                </div>
              </sc-for>
              <div style="color:#5A6E7A;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;margin-top:9px">Drafts can be written offline; the submission verbs stay online-only, so nothing enters a queue or a ledger from a disconnected laptop.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
